# Juodzbalis et al. (2026), MNRAS 546, stag086 (arXiv:2504.03551v2), published Fig. 19 (= arXiv v2 Fig. 20, fig:UVLF): UV LF of type-1 AGN hosts, JADES
# Redshift: 4 < z < 7; mean z of the 4<z<7 AGN listed in the paper (arXiv v2) = 5.3
# File label: z5pt0 kept as the nominal z~5 of the 4<z<7 bin (maintainer convention for wide JWST-AGN bins); mean z is given above
# Magnitude definition: total (AGN+host) M_UV (not nuclear M1450) -> M1500
# Phi convention: log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 mag^-1), asymmetric errors in dex (upper, lower); H0=70 inherited from the Bouwens+21 LF (paper itself uses Planck18)
# Note: no numerical table exists (none in the arXiv source either). Values are the vector coordinates of the green
#       points (whole sample) in the arXiv v2 figure; they agree with the earlier digitisation of the published Fig. 19
#       to < 1e-4 dex. Errors are Poisson, Phi*(1 +- 1/sqrt(N)) with N = 7, 9, 4.
# Note: Phi = f_AGN x Bouwens+21 galaxy UV LF with f_AGN = 5, 9, 2 per cent (likely lower limits);
#       bin edges from the plotted x-error bars: [-18.0,-18.75], [-18.75,-19.2], [-19.2,-20.4].
# Note: the paper shows large GOODS-N/GOODS-S cosmic variance and an L_bol dependence of this LF.
#
# M_UV    LogPhi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
-18.375  -3.715  0.139  0.206
-18.975  -3.735  0.125  0.176
-19.800  -4.695  0.176  0.301
